## Authorized bounded scope

The existing 2026-09-06 unified architecture section 11.7 mandates cooldown and Action Budget. This slice is ONLY an independent, in-memory admission policy for generic live Windows session canary attempts; historical recovery/graphics/Windows budget categories remain separate future work. No invented 45s or 3-attempt defaults. No runtime host, executor, selector, legacy BlueStacks/FF Guardian, UI, Windows mutation, History, Profile, benchmark lease or learning changes.

Files:
- Plan `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-19-track6-session-action-budget.md`.
- Production `src/FFPerformanceEngine.Core/Services/GenericGuardianSessionActionBudget.cs`.
- Test `tests/FFPerformanceEngine.Core.SelfTest/GenericGuardianSessionActionBudgetSelfTests.cs` plus single Program registration.

Contracts: the caller must supply positive cooldown, positive max attempts, and a session key with stable GameId, exact PID/path and nonempty owner-issued lifecycle GUID. `TryAdmit` independently checks Active/High, exact capturable target, same GameId/PID/path, supported anomaly family, reference-contained explicit LiveSafe action with nonblank Id, and immutable session identity. Lock-serialized admission charges one global canary-attempt slot immediately, applies cooldown per family+Action.Id, never charges cooldown/ineligible attempts, and refuses once budget exhausted even if cooldown expires. Explicit ResetSession affects only the exact epoch/target; owning host must first restore all active leases. A new lifecycle GUID distinguishes reused PIDs; the owning future host must never issue a fresh epoch per observation just to replenish quota. Clock/time arithmetic overflow fails closed. Policy grants no action-to-mutation authorization or stable process identity of its own.

